# `std::collections::vec_deque` — Circular Double-Ended Queue (`VecDeque`)

## 1. Design Intent & Rust `alloc::collections::VecDeque` Comparison

In Rust's `alloc::collections::VecDeque<T>`, wrap-around ring indexing (`head`, `len`, physical index modulo capacity) and split-slice reallocation (`handle_capacity_increase`) require delicate `unsafe` pointer copies across two disjoint ring segments.

In Jenny's `std::collections::vec_deque`, `VecDeque` composes `std::mem::raw_buf::RawBuf` and enforces ring-buffer wrap-around invariants at every entry and exit point:
- `invariant self.len >= 0 && self.len <= self.buf.cap`
- `invariant (self.buf.cap == 0 && self.head == 0) || (self.buf.cap > 0 && self.head >= 0 && self.head < self.buf.cap)`
- $O(1)$ amortized `push_front`, `push_back`, `pop_front`, `pop_back`, and random access `get(logical_idx)`
- Linearizing $2\times$ geometric growth (`grow_ring`) that unwraps split circular segments into a contiguous `[0 .. len)` layout (`head = 0`) and deterministically frees the old buffer.

## 2. Formal Interface & Contracts

```jenny
module std_collections_vec_deque

import std::mem::raw_buf

pub enum DequeError {
    EmptyDeque,
    IndexOutOfBounds,
    CapacityOverflow,
}

pub struct VecDeque {
    buf: RawBuf,
    head: i64 = 0,
    len: i64 = 0,

    invariant self.len >= 0 && self.len <= self.buf.cap
    invariant (self.buf.cap == 0 && self.head == 0) || (self.buf.cap > 0 && self.head >= 0 && self.head < self.buf.cap)
}

impl VecDeque {
    pub fn new() -> VecDeque
        effects []
        ensures result.len == 0 && result.buf.cap == 0 && result.head == 0

    pub fn with_capacity(cap: i64) -> VecDeque ! DequeError
        effects [AllocNative]
        requires cap >= 0 && cap <= 1048576 else DequeError.CapacityOverflow
        ensures result.len == 0 && result.buf.cap == cap && result.head == 0

    pub fn len(self) -> i64
        effects []
        ensures result == self.len

    pub fn capacity(self) -> i64
        effects []
        ensures result == self.buf.cap

    pub fn is_empty(self) -> bool
        effects []
        ensures result == (self.len == 0)

    pub fn grow_ring(mut self) -> i64 ! DequeError
        effects [Mutate, AllocNative]
        requires self.buf.cap < 1048576 else DequeError.CapacityOverflow
        ensures self.buf.cap > old(self.buf.cap) && self.head == 0 && self.len == old(self.len)

    pub fn push_back(mut self, val: i64) -> i64 ! DequeError
        effects [Mutate, AllocNative]
        requires self.len < 1048576 else DequeError.CapacityOverflow
        ensures self.len == old(self.len) + 1

    pub fn push_front(mut self, val: i64) -> i64 ! DequeError
        effects [Mutate, AllocNative]
        requires self.len < 1048576 else DequeError.CapacityOverflow
        ensures self.len == old(self.len) + 1

    pub fn pop_front(mut self) -> i64 ! DequeError
        effects [Mutate]
        requires self.len > 0 else DequeError.EmptyDeque
        ensures self.len == old(self.len) - 1

    pub fn pop_back(mut self) -> i64 ! DequeError
        effects [Mutate]
        requires self.len > 0 else DequeError.EmptyDeque
        ensures self.len == old(self.len) - 1

    pub fn get(self, logical_idx: i64) -> i64 ! DequeError
        effects []
        requires logical_idx >= 0 && logical_idx < self.len else DequeError.IndexOutOfBounds

    pub fn clear(mut self) -> i64
        effects [Mutate]
        ensures self.len == 0 && self.head == 0

    pub fn drop_deque(mut self) -> i64
        effects [Mutate, AllocNative]
        ensures self.len == 0 && self.buf.cap == 0 && self.head == 0
}

@example("EX-STD-DEQUE-01: VecDeque circular push_front, push_back, wrap-around 2x resize, and FIFO/LIFO pops") {
    var dq = VecDeque.with_capacity(4)!
    dq.push_back(10)!
    dq.push_back(20)!
    dq.push_front(5)!
    dq.push_front(1)!
    assert(dq.len() == 4)
    assert(dq.get(0)! == 1)
    assert(dq.get(1)! == 5)
    assert(dq.get(2)! == 10)
    assert(dq.get(3)! == 20)
    dq.push_back(30)!
    assert(dq.capacity() == 8)
    assert(dq.len() == 5)
    assert(dq.pop_front()! == 1)
    assert(dq.pop_back()! == 30)
    assert(dq.pop_front()! == 5)
    assert(dq.len() == 2)
    dq.drop_deque()
    assert(active_native_boxes() == 0)
}

@example("EX-STD-DEQUE-02: VecDeque rejects pop on empty and out-of-bounds logical index") {
    var dq = VecDeque.new()
    val e1 = dq.pop_front()
    assert(e1 is Err(DequeError.EmptyDeque))
    dq.push_back(42)!
    val e2 = dq.get(1)
    assert(e2 is Err(DequeError.IndexOutOfBounds))
    dq.drop_deque()
    assert(active_native_boxes() == 0)
}
```
